From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: sunxi: a733-r: Leave the I/O withstand voltage to
 the hardware

The A733 r-pinctrl shares the A523 r-pinctrl driver, and with it the
A523 way of programming the I/O withstand voltage: one bit per bank in
the register at 0x340, plus a control register at 0x344. On the A733,
SGPIO_POW_MOD_SEL at 0x340 has two bits per bank (PL at bits 1:0, PM
at bits 3:2; 0b00 and 0b10 select 3.3 V, 0b01 the adaptive mode, 0b11
1.8 V), and the manual documents no register at 0x344 (A733 User
Manual V1.00, 18.14.7.20, PDF p. 1836).

The Cubie A7S names no supply for these banks today, so nothing is
written yet. Without this, a 3.3 V supply for bank PL in the DT would
set bit 0 and turn the reset value 0b10 into 0b11, the 1.8 V mode on a
3.3 V bank, and a supply for bank PM would write into the PL field.

Give the A733 r-pinctrl its own description without the withstand
voltage handling, as the main A733 pin controller already does. The
withstand voltage stays as the boot chain set it.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: with a 1.8 V dummy supply named for bank PM
in a test DT, the withstand voltage register keeps the value of the boot
chain; without this patch the same DT clears a bit of the PL field.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun55i-a523-r.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun55i-a523-r.c b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun55i-a523-r.c
index cffc1e53eef1..21aaff247e07 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun55i-a523-r.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun55i-a523-r.c
@@ -30,11 +30,26 @@ static struct sunxi_pinctrl_desc a523_r_pinctrl_data = {
 	.pin_base = PL_BASE,
 };
 
+/*
+ * The A733 withstand voltage register has two bits per bank, so it cannot
+ * use the A523 one-bit layout: leave the withstand voltage to the hardware.
+ */
+static struct sunxi_pinctrl_desc a733_r_pinctrl_data = {
+	.irq_banks = ARRAY_SIZE(a523_r_irq_bank_map),
+	.irq_bank_map = a523_r_irq_bank_map,
+	.pin_base = PL_BASE,
+};
+
 static int a523_r_pinctrl_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
+	struct sunxi_pinctrl_desc *desc = &a523_r_pinctrl_data;
+
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(pdev->dev.of_node,
+				    "allwinner,sun60i-a733-r-pinctrl"))
+		desc = &a733_r_pinctrl_data;
+
 	return sunxi_pinctrl_dt_table_init(pdev, a523_r_nr_bank_pins,
-					   a523_r_irq_bank_muxes,
-					   &a523_r_pinctrl_data,
+					   a523_r_irq_bank_muxes, desc,
 					   SUNXI_PINCTRL_NCAT2_REG_LAYOUT);
 }
 
